{
 "summary": "Checkout failed (gateway 502s, 5xx ratio up to 81%) from about 00:20:22Z to 00:21:37Z because inventory POST /reserve became slow right after inventory 3.3.0 was deployed at 00:20:20Z. Orders timed out reserving inventory and returned 504, and the gateway surfaced 502. Errors ended around the inventory 3.3.1 deploy at 00:21:35Z, and gateway error ratio is now 0.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory release 3.3.0, deployed at 00:20:20Z, made POST /reserve slow (dominant self time about 2.46s avg, p95 up to 4.75s). This caused orders' reserve calls to time out (504), which propagated to gateway checkout as 502. What links the deploy to the failures: error logs began 2s after the deploy, all sampled error traces ran inventory 3.3.0 with most self time in inventory, and symptoms stopped right after 3.3.1 replaced 3.3.0.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "high",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-ebf632945eff",
   "ev-c8dd0e54519d",
   "ev-50374ccf6895",
   "ev-598e61f136b1",
   "ev-8d314bc61bf4"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders' reserve timeout (traces show about 2s end-to-end) converts inventory slowness into 504 failures instead of degraded latency. Inventory itself returned no 5xx.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c8dd0e54519d",
    "ev-50374ccf6895",
    "ev-c0a0cf40a875"
   ]
  }
 ],
